WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:16.031
Tina: I can't believe how far away the door seems.

2
00:00:16.032 --> 00:00:18.479
Danny: I'm tired of being tiny.

3
00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.517
I wish I were big.

4
00:00:20.518 --> 00:00:22.606
Bello: Me too.

5
00:00:22.607 --> 00:00:30.259
Chuck: You, me, and all of us!

6
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:32.468
Bello: How are we going to get in?

7
00:00:32.469 --> 00:00:34.857
Dave: There's no way we can lift it.

8
00:00:34.858 --> 00:00:37.491
Brad: Don't worry, we don't have to lift it.

9
00:00:37.492 --> 00:00:39.535
Dave: What do you mean?

10
00:00:39.536 --> 00:00:43.123
Brad: My dad always complains that it doesn't close right.

11
00:00:43.124 --> 00:00:47.822
Brad: There has to be a small gap somewhere.

12
00:00:47.823 --> 00:00:50.601
Danny: Well, I don't see any gap here.

13
00:00:50.602 --> 00:00:55.660
Tina: Let's try over there.

14
00:00:55.661 --> 00:00:57.572
Tina: There it is up ahead.

15
00:00:57.573 --> 00:00:59.154
Brad: I told you.

16
00:00:59.155 --> 00:01:00.449
Danny: Come on!

17
00:01:00.450 --> 00:01:13.113
Bello: Quick, let's get inside.

18
00:01:13.114 --> 00:01:16.225
Mrs. Rice: How did that sheet fly over my head?

19
00:01:16.226 --> 00:01:19.154
Mrs. Rice: It couldn't have been Tina or the giant.

20
00:01:19.155 --> 00:01:22.674
Mrs. Rice: I would have seen them.

21
00:01:22.675 --> 00:01:25.920
It must have been an invisible giant!

22
00:01:25.921 --> 00:01:27.989
Mrs. Rice: And it must be nearby!

23
00:01:27.990 --> 00:01:39.069
I have to warn someone.

24
00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:42.324
Bello: I can't believe how huge everything looks.

25
00:01:42.325 --> 00:01:44.779
It seemed so small before.

26
00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:48.813
Chuck: Danny, how are we going to be able to do anything here?

27
00:01:48.814 --> 00:01:50.996
Chuck: We're too tiny.

28
00:01:50.997 --> 00:01:54.780
Danny: We have our imaginations. Trust me.

29
00:01:54.781 --> 00:02:00.200
Danny: If we use our imaginations, we can do anything.

30
00:02:00.201 --> 00:02:03.305
Brad: First, we have to get the nano-putty.

31
00:02:03.306 --> 00:02:04.690
Dave: Where is it?

32
00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:07.769
Brad: It's in that filing cabinet.

33
00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:13.733
Tina: All right, everybody. Let's go.

34
00:02:13.734 --> 00:02:17.511
Chuck: Where did you get this magic putty from in the first place?

35
00:02:17.512 --> 00:02:20.393
Brad: My dad is a top secret scientist.

36
00:02:20.394 --> 00:02:24.364
Brad: I found the nano-putty one day when I was playing in the garage.

37
00:02:24.365 --> 00:02:27.129
Brad: I think my dad brought it home from his lab.

38
00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:30.790
Dave: Wow, that's pretty cool.

39
00:02:30.791 --> 00:02:32.904
Brad: We're almost there.

40
00:02:32.905 --> 00:02:44.152
Brad: The nano-putty is in the bottom drawer of the filing cabinet.

41
00:02:44.153 --> 00:02:45.905
Tina: What was that?

42
00:02:45.906 --> 00:02:50.460
Danny: A lightbulb just exploded!

43
00:02:50.461 --> 00:02:52.453
Chuck: We're under attack!

44
00:02:52.454 --> 00:02:54.856
Bello: Hurry, everybody!

45
00:02:54.857 --> 00:03:02.274
Tina: Watch out!

46
00:03:02.275 --> 00:03:04.486
Tina: Who could be attacking us?

47
00:03:04.487 --> 00:03:08.875
Chuck: It came from up there.

48
00:03:08.876 --> 00:03:10.907
Danny: It's just Brad's cat.

49
00:03:10.908 --> 00:03:13.827
It must have knocked some things off the table.

50
00:03:13.828 --> 00:03:15.764
Brad: She didn't mean to hurt us.

51
00:03:15.765 --> 00:03:23.342
She's a good kitty.
